{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1041322-ratribution-we-got-silver-homie","id":1041322,"title":"Ratribution :\" We Got Silver Homie! \"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-31T10:09:51-08:00","id":1041322,"title":"Ratribution :\" We Got Silver Homie! \"","content":"Hello everyone , Im so happy to have a place to discuss one of my loves in life.<br /> <br /> I've been playing werewolf the apocalypse since 1995 when I was only about 12 yrs old. I found out about werewolf after seeing a deck of RAGE cards being sold in Las Vegas at the Excalibur. I was entranced by the artwork. I wish I could say my nerd career started and branched out from that moment , but the truth is I only play werewolf and could care less about all other games. I used to post damn near a little over a decade ago on the white-wolf chat rooms as well.<br /> <br /> I wanted to share a chronicle I started with my old time child hood friends and open it up for critique and advice if that's ok. I tried talking to my wife about it but she thinks its ridiculous (which emboldens me more).<br /> <br /> <b>Chronicle name</b> : Ratribution :&quot; We Got Silver Homie! &quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Characters</b> : Death Squeek ( Rodens Knife Skulker) , Two-Tails (Metis Warrior) , and Bolthole Surfer (Rodens Tunnel Runner) , Nic Nac (Homid Engineer), Queso Freshness (Metis Twitcher)<ul><li><b>Death Squeek </b>- a quiet black oily rat that prefers to kill by crawling down a humans throat and suffocating them</li> </ul><ul><li><b>Two-Tails</b>- A metis &quot;wanna-be Nezumi&quot; with delusions that he is a master ninja under the tutelage of a high ranking Nezumi (which is a lie , he just likes kung fu exploitation films) He has two tails and refuses to use firearms , even if it means his own death. He has been tasked with raising and protecting the ratlings in the nest.</li> </ul><ul><li><b>Bolthole Surfer</b>- A rodens tunnel runner. He was infected with the birthing plague and left to have his brain melt away with fever , he finally collapsed onto a discarded Butthole Surfers CD to hallucinate into death , or survive the plague on top of this broken CD now sticky with his urine and vomit. He carries the CD to this day believing that it alone has the power to open boltholes for him through his travels. He prefers to kill by stabbing a pencil into humans ears.</li> </ul><ul><li><b>Nic Nac</b> - A homid engineer who was the janitor at a pentex subsidiary responsible for medical research. He enjoyed his late nights playing with the test rats and performing his own experiments with them using whatever discarded materials he could find. During a fit of madness a ratkin witness attacked him and infected him with the birthing plague. Nic Nac found himself a sweating gibbering mess deep in the subway system surrounded by the Chinatown subway nest. He was spared only by the interference of the Rat God through visions to Mint Stew and Bright Light .</li> </ul><ul><li><b>Queso Freshness</b>- A two headed Twitcher Metis who has been lost/abandoned in Pangea , the heads are side by side and constantly bicker and rip at the insides of each other faces. Belives himself to be a classic monster and enjoys stalking his victims when all the horror elements are just right in the environment for maximum effect and to spread fear through humanity. Also enjoys ripping humans in half and eating their guts like spaghetti while in crinos.</li> </ul><br /> <b>Location</b>: A small Nest deep in the Chinatown subway system in San Francisco. The nest is located in a small underground homeless hut put together with detritus and only accessible to Rodens Ratkin through a small rusting pipe sticking out of the roof of the homeless hut (maybe a 10 foot by 10 foot space). Inside the shitty homeless cubicle, propped against the wall is a mummified junkies corpse with his ribcage and dry guts split open. The mummified junkies lower jaw has been distended and held together with wires and safety pins amongst other junk. The lower jaw is where the new usurper Rat King named &quot;Mint Stew&quot; addresses her nest in rodens form, much like the pope would address his congregation. The mummified junkies hollowed out torso serves as Mint Stews &quot;right hand mans&quot; ritual staging area. a few bricks have been stacked inside the dry rotten junkies empty guts to serve as a form of an altar for &quot;Bright Light&quot; the nests premier shadow seer , a flamboyant ratkin that loves disco and rave , and subsequently has painted the insides of the homeless hut and his fur with black light paint and glowing stoner posters. A broken miniature disco ball (made for a cars rear view mirror) dangles from the inside ceiling of the dead junkies final rotten resting spot.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I hate super long posts (short attention span and what not) , so if anyone is interested to know more I'd love to explain the first session and open it up for advice and critique. If not I wont be butt hurt , I enjoy reading yalls posts at the end of the day anyway.<br /> <br /> Thanks for letting me be a part of this community!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T11:52:55-08:00","id":1041372,"title":"","content":"Good description of the Nest. I am curious, how does the Nest interact with the other Ratkin Nests in San Francisco Metropolitan Area? There should be anywhere from 9 Ratkin (if you are going with a ratio of 1:500,000) to 460 Ratkin (if you are going with a ratio of 1:10,000). In the former case, there should probably be thousands Rat Kinfolk for every Ratkin, as the local Ratkin have refrained from sharing the Birthing Plague for fear of killing off 90% of the Rat Kinfolk. In the latter case, there should be dozens of Rat Kinfolk for every Ratkin, as the Birthing Plague would have killed off most of the Rat Kinfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T12:47:40-08:00","id":1041416,"title":"","content":"I'll be honest I don't get caught up in all the math and whatnot , I sucked at school and usually just read WW books all day , but your input has intrigued me to really start thinking about.<br /> <br /> Anywho- In game, and for the story's purpose , the major Ratkin/Nest players for the rat pack characters are a group of Ratkin inhabiting the abandoned PAC BELL building in San Francisco who follow the Rat mother , and a nest located on Alcatraz island led by a plague lord , they are very isolationist and nobody really knows for sure what they are up too.<br /> <br /> As far as all the other &quot;nests&quot; I'll keep my players guessing. Of course they can use blood memory to recognize a fellow ratkin but even they don't know who's where all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T13:53:54-08:00","id":1041459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1041322-ratribution-we-got-silver-homie#post1041322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I hate super long posts (short attention span and what not) , so if anyone is interested to know more I'd love to explain the first session and open it up for advice and critique. If not I wont be butt hurt , I enjoy reading yalls posts at the end of the day anyway.<br /> <br /> Thanks for letting me be a part of this community!</div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome!<br /> Speaking just for me, I always enjoy reading about people's games. If you have the time and inclination I'd be interested in reading about how your sessions go.<br /> <br /> Adding to the thoughts about other nests: I find it helpful to not worry too much about the numbers of Ratkin in the city (assume there are plenty for whatever your game needs). That being said, it's fun to have at least 1 rival Nest set up. It adds another dynamic to the game and gives the players a rival group that they can work against that aren't also their allies. Ratkin can have rivals within their own Nest, but when it comes down to it, you generally can't go out and kill them just because they work against you. That is certainly a possibility for rival Nests.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T14:10:24-08:00","id":1041472,"title":"","content":"I plan on writing up how the first session went tomorrow.<br /> <br /> A few questions I have that I think my friends are trying to get over on me.<br /> <br /> Rat Mothers touch- My players have been trying to convince me that you can heal yourself with it , however I don't think that's how it works<br /> <br /> Also..<br /> <br /> The player who roleplays Queso Freshness says that his Fetish &quot;Ape skin&quot; will make him appear to others to only have one head. I didn't interpret it that way. To me he wouldn't look like a ratty shitbag bestial human , but he would still register as having two heads like a &quot;palatable&quot; Siamese twin for your average joe walking down the street.<br /> <br /> thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T14:15:14-08:00","id":1041475,"title":"","content":"You cannot overcome Metis disfigurements that easily, especially since both of the heads talk and bite. He chose his disfigurement, so he should just learn to deal with mortals noticing him. Anyway, he is a Twitcher, he should not care want mortals think of him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T14:24:40-08:00","id":1041481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1041322-ratribution-we-got-silver-homie?p=1041475#post1041475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You cannot overcome Metis disfigurements that easily, especially since both of the heads talk and bite. He chose his disfigurement, so he should just learn to deal with mortals noticing him. Anyway, he is a Twitcher, he should not care want mortals think of him.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree , I thought it was a bit cheesy myself","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T14:38:54-08:00","id":1041486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1041322-ratribution-we-got-silver-homie?p=1041472#post1041472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Rat Mothers touch- My players have been trying to convince me that you can heal yourself with it , however I don't think that's how it works</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct. Ratmother's Touch works like Mother's Touch and Mother's Touch says: &quot;This Gift may not heal the werewolf herself, spirits, or the undead.&quot;<br /> Pretty straight forward.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1041322-ratribution-we-got-silver-homie?p=1041472#post1041472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The player who roleplays Queso Freshness says that his Fetish &quot;Ape skin&quot; will make him appear to others to only have one head. I didn't interpret it that way. To me he wouldn't look like a ratty shitbag bestial human , but he would still register as having two heads like a &quot;palatable&quot; Siamese twin for your average joe walking down the street</div> </div> </div> </div>So I'm hoping you mean Monkey Puzzle (level 4 Fetish) and not Ape Skin (the level 1 Fetish). Ape Skin does nothing of the sort. Ape Skin does: &quot;When activated, the fetish \u2014 which takes the form of a scrap of ape or human skin tattooed with a glyph \u2014 makes the werewolf suffer no special damage from silver in Homid form, and also renders the Garou unable to regenerate in that form \u2014 just as though they were born homid.&quot;<br /> So going on the assumption that you meant Monkey Puzzle instead, it would work how the player envisions it, since the Puzzle specifically says :&quot;When activated, it causes all humans viewing the werewolf to believe her to be a normal human\u2026 regardless of the form she wears.&quot; <br /> <br /> The &quot;normal human&quot; part is the important one for this discussion. But yea, it you did mean the level 1 Fetish, then you may want to talk to the player and see if they want to invest in the level 4 one instead since it's closer to the effect the player was going for. It does nothing to protect from any sort of supernatural creature viewing you, but it's pretty perfect for going out in public in general.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T15:28:37-08:00","id":1041520,"title":"","content":"But conjoined twins are normal humans by WtA standards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T16:08:30-08:00","id":1041548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1041322-ratribution-we-got-silver-homie?p=1041520#post1041520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But conjoined twins are normal humans by WtA standards.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I can only speak for how I would run it. While conjoined twins are something that happen, what percentage of humans have that condition? I think the level 4 Fetish would cover that up and make the person appear &quot;normal&quot;. In this case, &quot;normal&quot; meaning typical human. I can certainly see the argument against, but for a level 4 Fetish that can hide a Crinos form strolling around, I see no reason for it to not hide a deformity.<br /> <br /> 2 follow up things. Again, this assumes the Fetish we're talking about is the Monkey Puzzle and not the Ape Skin Fetish.<br /> The Monkey Puzzle only works on humans. It shouldn't work on Supernaturals, and so relying on it for public outings all the time is inviting other supernaturals to take notice. That is ripe for story threads.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T16:12:23-08:00","id":1041551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1041322-ratribution-we-got-silver-homie?p=1041520#post1041520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But conjoined twins are normal humans by WtA standards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Debatable.<br /> <br /> There are not too many rules for the Monkey Puzzle, but the purpose of the fetish is to blend in. Being a two-headed dude or gal is not gonna help you do that. In any case, I don't think the fetish works by corresponding to a user's specific individual body parts- rather, it probably just provides a holistic illusion of a typical human.<br /> <br /> If your fera was scarred and missing a limb, I doubt that would be reflected in the illusion provided by the Puzzle.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Once again, beaten to the punch by Idpersona... I need to work on my words per minute or something. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T16:25:40-08:00","id":1041558,"title":"","content":"But the character gains too many advantages with two functional heads to not be penalized in some fashion just to balance him with the other characters. First, he could potentially survive beheading, which means that two decapitation attacks have to occur to have a confirmed kill (since he is Metis, he will never not have awesome soak and regeneration, so he could potentially regenerate the beheaded head as long as the other one survives). Second, he has two sets of sensory organs, which means sensory attacks need two confirmed successful attacks to cripple him. Third, he gets two sets of jaws, which means two aggravated bite attacks. I could probably think of more, but those three traits make it a very powerful mutation that should have equally powerful limitations (metis mutations should suck, not make you an even cooler superhuman).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T16:48:00-08:00","id":1041567,"title":"","content":"Guardians of the Caerns Pg. 101 &quot;Conjoined Twin Syndrome: When your parents mated the fertilized egg split, albeit imperfectly. Instead of having two identical metis twins, your mother bore you with a remnant of your twin still embedded in part of your body. Its pretty clear to any onlookers that you have parts of a metis fetus stuck into your flesh. While this causes you no physical difficulty, its a real problem on social situations. Add +2 diff on all social rolls that involve appearance and charisma&quot;<br /> <br /> So there is precedence for this, just as long as it doesn't grant a 2nd bite attack against opponents or survive decapitation (hell go for broke and say it can't shift and is always crinos...maybe an atrophied one but still).<br /> <br /> Btw, just want to say the intro (started in '95 due to a pack of Rage cards, and posting on the old white wolf chat sites....was totally the same way...'95, age 12, ect. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T17:37:49-08:00","id":1041588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1041322-ratribution-we-got-silver-homie?p=1041558#post1041558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the character gains too many advantages with two functional heads to not be penalized in some fashion just to balance him with the other characters. First, he could potentially survive beheading, which means that two decapitation attacks have to occur to have a confirmed kill (since he is Metis, he will never not have awesome soak and regeneration, so he could potentially regenerate the beheaded head as long as the other one survives). Second, he has two sets of sensory organs, which means sensory attacks need two confirmed successful attacks to cripple him. Third, he gets two sets of jaws, which means two aggravated bite attacks. I could probably think of more, but those three traits make it a very powerful mutation that should have equally powerful limitations (metis mutations should suck, not make you an even cooler superhuman).</div> </div> </div> </div>So we don't know the actual systems the OP is applying to having a second head. I would not make the assumptions you have. And having a second bite attack might mean absolutely nothing, if the character is still limited by action economy. If the character is treated as a singular entity for the purposes of attacks and perception checks, then the second head really doesn't provide any tangible benefits. It's just kind of hideous and annoying. Which is perfectly in line for the Monstrous Flaw, which is an acceptable Metis disfigurement.<br /> <br /> So really, I think it depends on how the ST goes about it. There are tons of ways to do so that don't amount to being &quot;cooler superhuman&quot;.<br /> <br /> And none of this has to do with how a level 4 Fetish works. If the ST approves a Fetish that will allow a Metis to situationally overcome their deformity then he/she already knows what they're getting into. And the Monkey Puzzle (again) only works on humans. The Metis character's deformity is still 100% visible to supernaturals. You are acting like the Fetish completely invalidates the Metis' deformity.<br /> <br /> As an alternate example: a Metis Uktena who is paraplegic can still learn Spirit of the Bird/Fish to fly or swim. There shouldn't be anything wrong with that. It <i>does</i> overcome the deformity's shortcoming <i>in certain situations</i>. That doesn't mean said Metis should be barred from learning those Gifts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T18:01:04-08:00","id":1041598,"title":"","content":"Well, that is a good point. Would the Fetish work against Fomori, Kinain, Kinfolk, Psychics, Sorcerers, etc? How human do you have to be to be human enough?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T19:43:03-08:00","id":1041643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1041322-ratribution-we-got-silver-homie?p=1041598#post1041598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that is a good point. Would the Fetish work against Fomori, Kinain, Kinfolk, Psychics, Sorcerers, etc? How human do you have to be to be human enough?</div> </div> </div> </div> So that's a lot more iffy. I've ruled if differently based on story needs. But as a general rule I let fomori see through it, being half spirit themselves. For others maybe base it on their highest path rating compared to the level of the Fetish. So if they have a 4 then have them roll off. If they have a 5, they are inhuman (or rather supernatural) enough to see through it.<br /> <br /> Ghouls are more tricky. I don't have an easy method off the top of my head. Maybe base it off of the Domitor's Gen?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T20:18:16-08:00","id":1041660,"title":"","content":"I do not know, that is an interesting question. Perhaps the highest level of Ghoul Discipline would be best?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T21:16:29-08:00","id":1041676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1041322-ratribution-we-got-silver-homie?p=1041660#post1041660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not know, that is an interesting question. Perhaps the highest level of Ghoul Discipline would be best?</div> </div> </div> </div>Then basically all ghouls count as normal humans for the sake of it. That is perfectly workable. You'd need a few hundred year old ghoul with a powerful domitor to have a chance to see through it. I think kinain fall roughly into the same area.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T21:59:57-08:00","id":1041685,"title":"","content":"Well, that depends on the Fae Blood Background of the Kinain. Kinain with Fae Blood 5 (the direct children of one or two Changelings) can and will likely develop Arts and Realms up to level 5, since Fae Blood acts as the cap for Glamour, Arts, and Realms. Of course, they will need a source of Glamour, but their Arts and Realms should be able to provide them with passive defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T23:16:20-08:00","id":1041709,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. Off the top of my head, I couldn't remember the systems for kinain. Would still be impossible for the majority of them to see through it (with this made up system) but I don't see that as too big of a deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T00:08:20-08:00","id":1041722,"title":"","content":"Somehow I never wanted to play Ratkin even though I love rats (we have pet rats at home) but this actually sounds like fun <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T06:59:02-08:00","id":1041797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1041322-ratribution-we-got-silver-homie?p=1041548#post1041548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I can only speak for how I would run it. While conjoined twins are something that happen, what percentage of humans have that condition? I think the level 4 Fetish would cover that up and make the person appear &quot;normal&quot;. In this case, &quot;normal&quot; meaning typical human. I can certainly see the argument against, but for a level 4 Fetish that can hide a Crinos form strolling around, I see no reason for it to not hide a deformity.<br /> <br /> 2 follow up things. Again, this assumes the Fetish we're talking about is the Monkey Puzzle and not the Ape Skin Fetish.<br /> The Monkey Puzzle only works on humans. It shouldn't work on Supernaturals, and so relying on it for public outings all the time is inviting other supernaturals to take notice. That is ripe for story threads.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was Ape Skin . The players got caught up on the part that says it makes you identical to a homid garou (I don't have my book with me right now). In any case I agree with yall. If it was a monkey puzzle then ok , but not ape skin.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also I don't allow the players of queso freshness to have two actions a turn. Not unless they spend rage or split actions. I probably shoulda mentioned that Queso Freshness is player by two people at the same time, two players that have vastly different outlooks on what actions to take at any given time.<br /> <br /> <br /> On another note , I don't take this ratkin game super serious (very tounge in cheek).<br /> <br /> In my opinion a ratkin game should be pretty wild and a little like being on a permanent LSD trip.<br /> <br /> Really this group I have we've always played as garou. Im kind of using this ratkin game to give the players insight into how garou would seem to outsiders , and to really give them a brutal look at their culture . The problem Im running into is that the majority of the group are playing their ratkin like they would a garou, and less like fanatic guerilla sociopaths.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T11:06:24-08:00","id":1041927,"title":"","content":"Now, I can get behind two players playing a conjoined twin. That offers many opportunities for very deep RP, especially if one of the twins starts to be attracted to humans while the other one is repulsed by humans, though I would have them be two separate characters instead of one shared character (though that is just a personal preference since there are no rules either way). And I agree that the standard Ratkin game should be hallucinogenic ride.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T12:39:14-08:00","id":1041962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1041322-ratribution-we-got-silver-homie?p=1041927#post1041927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I can get behind two players playing a conjoined twin.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually had this in a one-shot fera game set during the War of Rage. Two of the players were the different heads of the same Mokole (so, shared sheet. They did not really give a whit for the crunchy side of the game). The two bickered a fair amount and spat fire at Garou that got too close. It was fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T13:17:14-08:00","id":1041992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1041322-ratribution-we-got-silver-homie?p=1041797#post1041797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It was Ape Skin . The players got caught up on the part that says it makes you identical to a homid garou (I don't have my book with me right now). In any case I agree with yall. If it was a monkey puzzle then ok , but not ape skin.</div> </div> </div> </div>So yea. Completely agree with your call (for what little it counts).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1041322-ratribution-we-got-silver-homie?p=1041797#post1041797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also I don't allow the players of queso freshness to have two actions a turn. Not unless they spend rage or split actions. I probably shoulda mentioned that Queso Freshness is player by two people at the same time, two players that have vastly different outlooks on what actions to take at any given time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds perfectly workable.<br /> Honestly, if it's 2 players then 2 actions a turn would be fine by me. Whatever works for your play group. Sounds fun though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1041322-ratribution-we-got-silver-homie?p=1041797#post1041797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> On another note , I don't take this ratkin game super serious (very tounge in cheek).<br /> <br /> In my opinion a ratkin game should be pretty wild and a little like being on a permanent LSD trip.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds perfect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1041322-ratribution-we-got-silver-homie?p=1041797#post1041797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Really this group I have we've always played as garou. Im kind of using this ratkin game to give the players insight into how garou would seem to outsiders , and to really give them a brutal look at their culture . The problem Im running into is that the majority of the group are playing their ratkin like they would a garou, and less like fanatic guerilla sociopaths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not every Ratkin needs to be like that. But from your character descriptions it sounds like you have a nice mix of character types. It might just take the players a few sessions to warm up to the idea of how you expect the game to go. And you may also end up having to alter your vision a bit. It happens. Keep us updated if you feel like it. Above all, have fun with it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T22:45:31-08:00","id":1042240,"title":"","content":"Additionaly you made me look up some basics about Ratkin yesterday <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I guess I will be more open to playing them in the future than I was so far. And no, I cant even really tell what made me not want to play them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T23:28:14-08:00","id":1042248,"title":"","content":"Intriguing! Nice nest description, gotta steal that hollowed out Junkie for a game. :P<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T02:31:23-08:00","id":1042302,"title":"","content":"Perhaps it was their mistreatment of the Homid Ratkin and Human Kinfolk? Anyway, the strange thing about the Ratkin is that their Kinfolk do not directly effect their population but, unlike the Corax, it is the Kinfolk who sacrifice to become Ratkin. When 90% are potentially killed by the Birthing Plague, 'reproductive' strategy becomes important. If you go with a K strategy, you select the best Kinfolk, with the highest Stamina, so they have a good chance of surviving even if they are rejected by the Birthing Plague. If you go with an r strategy, you do not care and you let 90% of the Kinfolk die.<br /> <br /> For Nests that go with K, you have low Ratkin population, but you should get better individual training. For Nests that go r strategy, you have high Ratkin populations, but you have poorer individual training. I think that default would be strong r, so I would give beginning Ratkin from strong-K Nests large bonuses to reflect the differences (+1/1/1 Attributes, +2/2/2 Abilitues, +3 Level One Gifts, and +6 Freebie Points). It would be the difference between 'lots of ninja' and 'one ninja'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T07:07:58-08:00","id":1042393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1041322-ratribution-we-got-silver-homie?p=1042302#post1042302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Perhaps it was their mistreatment of the Homid Ratkin and Human Kinfolk? Anyway, the strange thing about the Ratkin is that their Kinfolk do not directly effect their population but, unlike the Corax, it is the Kinfolk who sacrifice to become Ratkin. When 90% are potentially killed by the Birthing Plague, 'reproductive' strategy becomes important. If you go with a K strategy, you select the best Kinfolk, with the highest Stamina, so they have a good chance of surviving even if they are rejected by the Birthing Plague. If you go with an r strategy, you do not care and you let 90% of the Kinfolk die.</div> </div> </div> </div>90% of Kin don't die from the Birthing Plague. Even in the old setup, they didn't. But especially in the new setup (as of W20). This is the System now: &quot;the ritemaster rolls Wits + Rituals (difficulty 7). The victim must make a Stamina roll with a difficulty equal to (10 \u2013 the ritemaster\u2019s successes) to survive the hallucinations, visions, and fevers of the Birthing Plague.&quot;<br /> So lets assume the Ritesmaster gets on average 3 successes. That means the Kin rolls stamina at dif 7 to survive. With a Stamina of 2, that leaves the kin a 56% chance of success (not dying). If you go with the Ritesmaster getting 2 successes instead then the chance of a 2 Stamina Kin passing the roll is still 46%.<br /> Now the chances of the Kin coming out of the other side as a Ratkin are 10-20% based on breed. But all in all I think the actual attrition rate is much lower than 90%.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1041322-ratribution-we-got-silver-homie?p=1042302#post1042302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> For Nests that go with K, you have low Ratkin population, but you should get better individual training. For Nests that go r strategy, you have high Ratkin populations, but you have poorer individual training. I think that default would be strong r, so I would give beginning Ratkin from strong-K Nests large bonuses to reflect the differences (+1/1/1 Attributes, +2/2/2 Abilitues, +3 Level One Gifts, and +6 Freebie Points). It would be the difference between 'lots of ninja' and 'one ninja'.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no need to offer boosts like that (imo). The starting character is already assumed to have superior training and/or genetics. If anything, I would keep the Nest-r Ratkin base kinfolk stat spreads (6/4/3, 11/7/4) and give them free dots in the Kinfolk and Nest backgrounds and call it a day. And even that I think goes further than necessary. There is zero reason to give a &quot;stronger breeding&quot; Nest a +54 Freebie Point advantage. That's insane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T11:26:40-08:00","id":1042527,"title":"","content":"<u><b>INTRO: (sorry for the length hope yall enjoy, if not sorry for being a dickhead)</b></u><br /> Our tale begins with the exodus of two ratkin in the year 1800 and some shit or other. These Two Vermin are not particularly competitive or cunning\u2026.. and shit was getting too hot back in San Francisco\u2019s Chinatown with all the competition for real estate. Especially from the Rat Kings mothers second cousins brothers aunts daughter\u2026..Mint Stew, a violent maniac whose rage and machavellian schemes could only be soothed by Chinese opium\u2026... <br /> Work Smarter not harder both Ratkin figure\u2026.. It just wasn\u2019t worth it to stick around\u2026.<br /> These two fools decide to make a break for the wooded mountains north of the city in an effort to establish their own nest in a small mountain mining town reminiscent of a low budget spaghetti western\u2026..<br /> \u2026\u2026..But how were they going to get there? Travel through the woods, swim across the bay, take your chances in the storm umbra\u2026\u2026\u2026. no fucking way\u2026..<br /> \u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026&quot; I know a guy\u2026&quot; Death Squeak hisses\u2026.it was the only thing he had said all day\u2026.Two Tails shook his head and rubbed his tails nervously &quot; \u2026\u2026.Im not payin\u2026.!&quot;<br /> <br /> <b><u>CHAPTER 1 : The Death of Ten Thunders</u></b><br /> Death Squeak and Two Tails (in Rodens form) are clumsily hitching a ride in the talons a great greasy black bird. The trio glides and dips , and almost crashes into the tops of large redwoods more times than they can count , but the shit is fun nonetheless, well fun for Death Squeak anyway. <br /> The trio fly\u2019s at an upward angle towards where they think this gold mining settlement is , or at least where the newspaper in the gutter said it would be. They cover great stretches of dark mountainous forest after crossing a body of water and catch sight of a pillar of smoke rising just up over the next ridge. Funny, they can\u2019t smell the smoke.<br /> Death Squeek in his excitement to settle a new home, struggles to get a better view from the grips of the birds talons when &quot;PLOOP!&quot;<br /> MOTHERFUCKER DONE SLIPS OUT THE BIRDS GRASP AND DOES A SLOW MOTION FREE FALL (IN RODENS FORM) AGAINST THE BACKDROP OF A COLD FULL MOON ( falling silently like that German dude in Die Hard). <br /> TWO TAILS desperately wraps his two tails around the birds neck in an effort to strangle / violently guide the bird downward to catch his friend\u2026\u2026..but this shit doesn\u2019t work , and now all three dummies are tumbling to their demise\u2026\u2026.<br /> After a brief black out, Death Squeek and Two Tails (both in rodens form) rise and wrinkle their noses and whiskers at the cold air. There\u2019s a lot of those half assed black birds perched all over the damn place squawking bullshit at each other and causing a racket\u2026...<br /> This looks like the small western gold mining town, but there\u2019s no scent, and the shit looks deserted\u2026... Furthermore, they don\u2019t feel like the crash landing did shit to them physically.<br /> They peer over the edge of the roof and realize they are on top of the towns Saloon, only to spy The scattered shadows and remains of dead horses, throttled pieces of what was once many whores and what appears to be men\u2019s shredded remains and rusting mining equipment/tools. From this vantage point they also spy what look like highlighter yellow neon slugs inching over the littered remains.<br /> Both Ratkin shrug and decide to take inventory of the new spot and investigate\u2026.without people , there won\u2019t be much food , but Two Tails figures there enough meat to go around for a while\u2026. The duo sneak down rafters and into broken windows into the lightless interior of the saloon. Still no scents, and still no movement noticed inside the saloon.<br /> Two Tails is starving\u2026.. He sniffs at a sloppy Highlighter neon yellow slug settled on a hunk of cool meat and nibbles on it\u2026\u2026. it crunches like Styrofoam packing peanuts. Two Tails spits out the tasteless worm.<br /> Death Squeek shifts to Homid and rummages through the area, stepping over broken glass, pools of dark fluid that have congealed sticky and various chunks of flesh and bone. Both Rats notice rends and gouges in the floor and walls\u2026 Two Tails finds a severed hand attached to a Colt pistol and starts gnawing on the cold stiff waxy fingers , he\u2019s careful to use one of his tails to move the gun away from his meal (like a child would remove a long hair from his porkchop), It\u2019s been a perilous flight after all\u2026..<br /> Behind the bar, Death Squeek finds a small wooden box ornately carved with a red velvet interior. It contains 6 silver bullets. He continues to rummage a gold nugget here and a gold nugget there and sets himself up with a round of whiskey shots to bless his new home.<br /> The air is cold and chill, but not damp\u2026. Two Tails shifts to homid as well and wipes his mouth of black-red slime\u2026 &quot;something is off with this place, that meat shoulda tasted a lot worse\u2026..it didn\u2019t taste like nothing?!?!&quot; \u2026\u2026..Death Squeek doesn\u2019t respond except to shake the wooden box of bullets and motion for Two Tails to give him the pistol. Two Tails karate kicks the gun disgustedly towards Death Squeek and goes to peer outside a blood stained and bullet ridden window.<br /> The silence outside the saloon is interrupted by a thunderous Howl that causes dust to kick up on the road. The few bits of broken glass clinging to existence here and there vibrate from the force of the howl and crash to the floor\u2026.<br /> Death Squeek and Two Tails look at each other and begin to shiver excitedly. Two Tails says he can see something down the dirt road clinging to the shadows of the edge of the ghost town. &quot;I can\u2019t get a read on it\u2026.&quot; Two Tails begins shifting into his wiry Crinos Ratman form still trying to stay hidden. <br /> Death Squeek feels his heart go into overdrive\u2026.. races to the blood stained window fumbles with loading the pistol with the silver ammo and trying to shift into crinos all at the same time\u2026\u2026\u2026.(botch) he trips over a cadavers torso and goes tumbling through the window that Two Tails was looking through ,scattering glass and clumsily rolling head over tail into the middle of the dusty street. <br /> Immediately the large shadowed being at the edge of the town comes racing on all fours full blast towards the rat creature on the ground with dust settling around him. Panicked Death Squeek grabs the pistol with his tail and retreats, bounding like a gymnast and jumping back through the window.<br /> Both Ratkin hide in the darkness of the saloon / impromptu miners morgue and try to get a good look at the Crinos Garou outside the saloon pawing and sniffing at the spot where Death Squeek just made his presence known (I love botches). The black and tan wolf man rears back on all fours and roars displeasure into the night sky pleading to the full moon in a savage prayer and announces himself\u2026.<br /> <b>&quot;I\u2026\u2026. TEN THUNDERS!...... I ONCE CALL\u2026.. ONE THUNDER!....... YOU NOT BELONG!&quot;</b><br /> Two Tails turns to look at Death Squeek and both start confused shaking. \u2026..&quot;We speak Garou?!&quot;\u2026.. . Death Squeek counts to ten on each clawed finger his eyes going wide like two black eight balls (Death Squeeks player spends a wp). Death Squeek shrugs off the willies and readies the pistol in a tight grip. He inches towards the stairs going up to the second floor of the saloon with Two Tails right behind moonwalking backwards feeling for where he needs to step by using his two tails like a blind dude with a stick. He keeps his glossy black eyes on TEN THUNDERS outside as much as he can\u2026..<br /> Numerous far off howls from higher up on the forested mountain are shouted to the heavens and cascade down through the ravaged mining town\u2026\u2026\u2026.they are responding to Ten Thunders howl of introduction\u2026.believing it was intended for them\u2026\u2026\u2026...<br /> &quot;WE HERE!&quot;\u2026\u2026. the other howls on the mountain respond to TEN THUNDERS angrily &quot;WHO YOU!&quot;\u2026.. &quot;GET OUT!&quot;\u2026\u2026. &quot;DON\u2019T COME !&quot; \u2026&quot;LEEEEEEEEEAAAAVE!!&quot;\u2026. &quot; WE KILL&quot;\u2026.&quot;MY HOME!&quot;\u2026\u2026\u2026<br /> Ten Thunders rolls his shoulders back and stands proud revealing two long black braids connected to TWO blue human skulls dangling against his ritually scarred chest. Ten Thunders faces the direction of the response on the mountain.<br /> Ten Thunders negotiates with the garou of the mountain to admit him into their territory. He has heard from the spirits of the mountain how they cleansed this town from the face of Gaia and he wishes to join in the Glory. <br /> Ten Thunders pledges to shred these filthy creatures whatever they may be. they seem to have manifested among the carnage of the monkeys town so close to their bawn. Ten Thunders proposes the Mountain garou allow him entrance to their caern if he does his duty\u2026.. <br /> The two ratkin huddle into a whores bedroom on the second story staring out a broken window down at Ten Thunders and eavesdropping on his conversation. <br /> &quot;\u2026Ssssssstuck\u2026\u2026Stuck\u2026.. sssssStuck\u2026.&quot; Death Squeek chitters repeatedly aiming at Ten Thunders.<br /> &quot; I don\u2019t wanna live here anymore\u2026.&quot; Mumbles Two Tails\u2026..<br /> Two Tails readies his Pain Dagger\u2026closes his beady eyes and mutters some low rate strip mall karate class prayerto Rat God under his fetid rotten flesh breathe\u2026\u2026\u2026<br /> One\u2026\u2026 single \u2026..old\u2026.gutteral\u2026. howl erupts from the trees in response to Ten Thunders\u2019 proposal silencing the rest of the unseen mountain garou\u2026<br /> &quot; PROCEED TEN THUNDERS SON OF FENRIS\u2026..&quot;<br /> \u2026\u2026A Lupine grin creeps across Ten Thunders wet Muzzle revealing thick glistening ivory teeth dripping crystal clear strands of saliva. His head turns slowly towards the saloon.<br /> &quot;POW!!&quot;<br /> From out the whores window on the second story of the saloon a bright flash and burst of smoke. Death Squeek (who somehow still understands the Garou tongue) levies a shot on Ten Thunders catching the Garou solidly in the chest. <br /> Burning with hatred and searing silver pain and eager prove his worth to the Mountain Garou, Ten Thunders SWINGS INTO BATTLE FERVOR and crashes through the double doors of the saloon flinging insults, firing arcs of spittle, and tossing chairs and tables, in a mad search for prey. Ten Thunders flips and smashes a piano. kicking up pieces of rotting meat and empty glass bottles\u2026<br /> \u2026\u2026..Ten Thunders pauses , heaving, frustrated , while blood crusted poker cards start to fall back and forth around his hulking mass like red dry leaves\u2026.morbid confetti amidst his violent performance\u2026<br /> Death Squeek runs further back into the second story bedroom of the saloon and shields himself along the wall, sticking his new pistol out towards the bottom of the stairwell. When Ten Thunders approaches tossing tables and chairs and kicking up body parts Death Squeek shoots two more times catching Ten Thunders once and missing the second shot. Ten Thunders oblivious to the pain leaps back onto the bar and reaches up trying to bring the second story down and shield himself from another dose of lunas metal. Two Tails begins stabbing through the floor trying to hit Ten Thunders as he starts tearing away floor boards and raining down wooden splinters\u2026\u2026<br /> Two Tails skinny dirty foot is caught in a massive bear trap of a clawed hand. TWO TAILS shrieks and slashes wildly at TEN THUNDERS arm while evacuating his bowels.<br /> Death Squeek sensing an opportunity leaps down the stair well in an amazing act of bravery\u2026.. Sneaks up behind the thrashing Ten Thunders who is tearing lumber off the ceiling and says---<br /> &quot;WE GOT SILVER HOMIE!&quot;\u2026\u2026..aaaaaaand pumps a hot silver round into the back of Ten Thunders skull\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026.his body crumbling onto the bar\u2026\u2026lights out\u2026. surrounded by wooden wreckage and broken bottles of whiskey.<br /> Two Tails looks down through the wreckage of the second story bedroom floor \u2026..hyper \u2026..yelling\u2026..and soiled \u2026.. &quot;I GOT HIM! RAT GODS BLESSING I GOT HIM!!! &quot;\u2026\u2026 He stands proudly, Pain Dagger in hand, dripping hot garou blood\u2026.. Two Tails does an unnecessary front flip ninja style down the impromptu hole in the floor boards, and lands Ten Thunders shrinking mass (both tails erect with excitement)<br /> Death Squeek shakes his head like a disappointed older brother and stares down at Ten Thunders ,whose body is reverting to a large black and tan wolf.<br /> Two Tails mistakes the body shrinking as a sign of life and begins wildly stabbing the wolf\u2019s body in a very un-ninja like manner like he\u2019s an extra in some rejected Tarantino film. <br /> Death Squeek goes to peek his large rat head out the window he tumbled out just moments earlier before all this chaos took place\u2026. <br /> The perched murders of black birds all freeze silent and in shock at the sight of the Rat man\u2019s curious head poking out the broken saloon window\u2026\u2026\u2026. they throw their avian heads back and cackle in a parody of laughter at seeing a Ratkin emerge victorious .<br /> &quot; THIS DOGS STILL MOVING!@&amp;%$%! &quot;\u2026. TWO-TAILS SHREIKS AT HIS NESTMATE!<br /> Death Squeek frowns and stomps heavily back to his kill rearing his hand back like a drunk wife beater and begins pistol whipping TEN-THUNDERS lifeless wolf head\u2026.. TWO-TAILS resumes chopping up some canine sushi\u2026...just to be sure\u2026\u2026\u2026<br /> The Saloon fills with a fountain of fine red mist emerging from every unnecessary wound occurring on Ten Thunders steaming body.<br /> Covered in gore, fur and red mess, The Ratkin duo hear a loud REVERBRATING&quot; BOOM!&quot; out in the atmosphere\u2026... they both look up confused and are launched skyward as if they were connected to a bungee cord pulling them back up to a platform they NEVER jumped off of. They both blast upwards Smashing into and shattering the roof of the saloon like two skinny red greasy biological rockets.<br /> Once they hit a certain height (against the backdrop of Luna \u2026..E.T. STYLE)\u2026. they pause suspended in glorious moonlight\u2026.both Rat Men share a worried look\u2026\u2026.<br /> aaaaaaaaaaaaaaand both begin a rapid descent back to earth\u2026\u2026<br /> On impact with the ground both Ratkin sink softly , swallowed up by the dusty jello pudding like dirt road\u2026 \u2026..they black out\u2026\u2026.<br /> \u2026\u2026.Surrounded by darkness \u2026\u2026\u2026. Dazed and Confused\u2026\u2026. Two Tails and Death Squeek hear the chastising echoes of their nest mate\u2026\u2026\u2026. Bolthole Surfer\u2026\u2026He sounds like a frustrated 3<sup><span style=\"font-size:10px\">rd</span></sup> grade at risk teacher ready to quit her job.<br /> <b>&quot;ARE YOU FUCKIN SERIOUS!!?!?! GET YOUR RATGODDAMN HEADS IN THE GAME! HEY! HEEEY RAT GOD HELP ME!!!! YOU IDIOTS ARE GOING TO RUIN THE WHOLE PLAN!!!!!!!!*&amp;^</b><br /> <br /> End of chapter one<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T17:44:34-08:00","id":1043274,"title":"","content":"Im the only die hard werewolf fan in my playing group...the rest of the guys play all sorts of other stuff so I have to try and do stuff to keep them committed and interested besides just the game session. I started making their characters out of clay.<br /> <br /> Do any of y'all other ST do something similar to maintain interest from your group?<br /> <br /> Heres an example of one I did for Bolthole Surfer<br /> <img src=\"http://i1248.photobucket.com/albums/hh497/ALRO00/boltholesurfer_zpszryeapee.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T17:48:34-08:00","id":1043276,"title":"","content":"This is the unfinished Queso Freshness.........<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i1248.photobucket.com/albums/hh497/ALRO00/queso2_zpsfrzhmwdv.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i1248.photobucket.com/albums/hh497/ALRO00/quesofreshness_zpsujbtwiia.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T18:00:52-08:00","id":1043280,"title":"","content":"Those are awesome! Great job.<br /> <br /> I end up with folders and folders full of pictures for every named NPC my group comes across, and I encourage (usually via XP) my players to go out and find pictures for their characters. We have a social media page, where the players can put up in-character comments on the various NPCs between sessions if they want to. Depending on the player it's hit or miss. Some couldn't care less, but some of them really get into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T18:08:25-08:00","id":1043285,"title":"","content":"dude a social media page is a great idea!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T18:16:45-08:00","id":1043287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1041322-ratribution-we-got-silver-homie?p=1043285#post1043285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">dude a social media page is a great idea!!</div> </div> </div> </div>If you have players who are interested, it makes for a great addition. And players can drop in and interact at any point during the week(s) between sessions.<br /> <br /> It was kind of sad when I/we migrated to the newer big social media site and I basically left years of work/record behind. I can still log in there (the old one) but the interface isn't as good as it used to be and so I don't bother unless I have to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T18:29:07-08:00","id":1043293,"title":"","content":"Question dude: If after or during the War of Rage most Ratkin evacuated earth and went into the Umbra , but now they are &quot;returning&quot; to earth , wouldn't they be purely spirit from having been in the Umbra all this time? Also how would they breed in the Umbra? Or would they just make metis? <br /> <br /> This has bugged me for some time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T19:55:04-08:00","id":1043325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1041322-ratribution-we-got-silver-homie?p=1043293#post1043293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question dude: If after or during the War of Rage most Ratkin evacuated earth and went into the Umbra , but now they are &quot;returning&quot; to earth , wouldn't they be purely spirit from having been in the Umbra all this time? Also how would they breed in the Umbra? Or would they just make metis? <br /> <br /> This has bugged me for some time.</div> </div> </div> </div>If a remember correctly, one of the freak factor levels said something about spirit parentage. I know there was a merit (Wendigo maybe) that said similar.<br /> Honestly though, story trumps rules and the Nuwisha hide in the Umbra en masse too. <br /> <br /> So... just because? Helpful, I know.<br /> <br /> And slight correction. During the Way of Rage, most Ratkin died. Some fled to the Umbra (and managed to escape). But those in the Umbra have been breeding and waiting... and changing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 02-03-2017, 10:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T23:51:25-08:00","id":1044411,"title":"","content":"Great sculptures there! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> By now we have a collection of plush toys roughly representing each character that was or is part of the Sentai in our Hengeyokai game. A shark for the Same Bito (though its not a hammerhead like that character), a rat for the Nezumi ex-member, a dragon for a Zong Lung ex-member, .... We're just lacking ravens, a fox and a spider.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T09:31:23-08:00","id":1044564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1041322-ratribution-we-got-silver-homie?p=1044411#post1044411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great sculptures there! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> By now we have a collection of plush toys roughly representing each character that was or is part of the Sentai in our Hengeyokai game. A shark for the Same Bito (though its not a hammerhead like that character), a rat for the Nezumi ex-member, a dragon for a Zong Lung ex-member, .... We're just lacking ravens, a fox and a spider.</div> </div> </div> </div>do you mind telling me a little bit about how the nezumi is played/presented/portrayed in your game?<br /> <br /> Also thank you kindly for the compliment (I don't know what I did, but the pictures went missing)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12902,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","user":"WISDOMINCHAINS","date":". 02-06-2017, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T22:43:11-08:00","id":1044921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1041322-ratribution-we-got-silver-homie?p=1044564#post1044564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> do you mind telling me a little bit about how the nezumi is played/presented/portrayed in your game?<br /> <br /> Also thank you kindly for the compliment (I don't know what I did, but the pictures went missing)</div> </div> </div> </div>I can still see them.<br /> <br /> About that Nezumi:<br /> He died when we fought a powerful bane (dont remember exactly what it was called) and tried to sneak up on it from behind, none of us remembering that the thing was supposed to know and see anything in his domain so there was no surprise when he attacked which was his demise.<br /> He actually was a storyteller character but a member of the Sentai nonetheless. He was our Leave, a young, ugly (appearance 1) guy really upholding the low warfare like Nezumi often do, shaking his head at the Same Bito Fist's concept of honorable combat . A showoff at times (no, I wont just jump down there, I'll do the cool thing with a somersault and whatnot and hope I don't botch the roll) and kind of a sneaky bastard (think ninja guy minus the all black dress and sword. He used sai instead) but also always good for a funny and snide comment. Often in little squabbles with our Tengu Mirror who used to throw random stuff at him in such situations after particularly well placed comments.<br /> He also didn't hold human live in high regard (&quot;they're only human after all...&quot;) and was by far the most prone to killing people without much thought. An attitude that sometimes would earn him conflict/discussions from the rest of the Sentai and something like a shrug from my character (the Ananasi). For example the Kitsune once found him after following him into a criminal-owned ship he was sent to scout. He was in rodens form, snuck right into a drug lab on the lower decks, happily adding poison into their mix.<br /> <br /> EDIT: His Hengeyokai name was &quot;Death of the thousand eyes&quot; after he managed to kill a large spider spirit (orb weaver? I always mix up the names of the various spider spirits) when we were trying to rescue another Sentai that had fallen prey to spider spirits who were trying to block the path to an old totem's realm with webs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11694,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","user":"Hexer","date":". 02-07-2017, 08:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T09:55:40-08:00","id":1045178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1041322-ratribution-we-got-silver-homie?p=1044411#post1044411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great sculptures there! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> By now we have a collection of plush toys roughly representing each character that was or is part of the Sentai in our Hengeyokai game..</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have any pictures? I really like seeing other peoples WoD inspired art/crafts. I don't know if this forum is big on that stuff or if a thread is already dedicated to it , but I'd love to see them.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T22:29:33-08:00","id":1045622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1041322-ratribution-we-got-silver-homie?p=1045178#post1045178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you have any pictures? I really like seeing other peoples WoD inspired art/crafts. I don't know if this forum is big on that stuff or if a thread is already dedicated to it , but I'd love to see them.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well its not EXACTLY &quot;WoD inspired art/crafts&quot; since 2 of the things are just simple plush toys that were bought (the dragon was bought for another reason but happened to kind of fit the characters war-form, the shark was bought when our Same Bito player found it). The rat is the only thing actually hand-crafted from an online friend for my girlfriend (we have pet rats) and when it arrived we realised it could be taken to resemble the Nezumi character (who was already dead by then). It all kinda spawned the idea that we need to find a plush spider, fox and ravens to complete the collections <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I can take pics though. We have the rat at home, the dragon is at our ST's who I'll see for a game session friday night and with a bit of luck the Same Bito player will bring the shark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T04:36:01-08:00","id":1047150,"title":"","content":"Here are those pics.<br /> Daw (Zong Lung) and Kong (Same Bito)<br /> <img src=\"https://img4.picload.org/image/ropgiaal/kleinimg_20170210_192637.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Kong and his mate<br /> <img src=\"https://img4.picload.org/image/ropgiorr/kleinimg_20170210_192702.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"l